If all information is missing for a given case, there is no statistical basis for assigning a likelihood. FIML needs some "knowns" in each case. If you want those cases included in your analysis, you may be able to accomplish this using auxiliary variables where you do have data for those cases. But you will have to include those variables in your analysis somehow.

