The R-squared for H2 is nearly 100%, matching the near-zero standardized residual variance.  I expect this makes it hard to estimate related parameters when you are identifying the model by fixing H2's residual variance to 1.  Try instead fixing its first loading to 1 and freely estimating its residual variance (manually doing so in the syntax will override the std.lv <http://std.lv>=TRUE argument for that factor).  I wonder whether your estimated residual variance might end up being negative...

