That is not correct. ML estimation requires multivariate normality. Multinormality means that higher order moments of the data beyond the second can be computed from lower order moments, so that a covariance matrix in itself is a sufficient statistic. Other estimators for structural equation models do not require multinormality. So the distributional requirement is tied to the estimator, not to the form of the model, or even to the use of common factors rather than, say, composites, to represent the unobserved variables.

