Dear Torrence and Eaindray,

My own simulations (unpublished) :

pop.mod = '

F1 =~ 0.5*x1 + 0.6*x2 + 0.7*x3

F2 =~ 0.5*x4 + 0.6*x5 + 0.7*x6

F1 ~~ 0.5*F2

'

So, for 6 items, even a n=60 works quite well for 5-categories… for normal data…

For biased data (using the Finney &DiStefano cutting rule |sk|<=3, |Ku|<=7:

